<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Oybin–Gratzer Felsen–Töpfer–Scharfenstein circuit — Gratzer–Töpfer–eastern rocks–Scharfenstein base circuit [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Start beside Oybin station and follow Goldbach/Talweg through Gratzer to Töpfer plateau and its unnamed stair-accessed return viewpoint. Continue through the full eastern rock passage past Böhmisches Fenster, Rübezahl, Hussitenriff, Feuerstein, Onkel/Tante, kleine Eisrinne and Kleine Felsengasse to Scharfenstein’s base; return past Green Riff. The optional summit is excluded. This roughly 6.7 km circuit remains demanding, with uneven steps and exposure. Use suitable footwear, dry snow- and ice-free daylight, sure-footedness and extra time. Markings are incomplete. Stay on protected paths, do not climb off-path or alter rocks, and cross roads and railway carefully. Closed, forbidden or unsafe required passages make the full itinerary unavailable. Approximate 436 m ascent/descent and 165 minutes are planning estimates.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Approximate route for planning; follow signs and check current conditions on the ground.

